ao_coreaudio: stop passing a channel layout as a channel map (macOS 27)

Backport of upstream 3dae21b1ed ("ao_coreaudio: remove misusage of audio
unit channel map API", 2026-10-24, fixes mpv #18384). Since 06fe665b78
(Jan 2025) mpv hands kAudioOutputUnitProperty_ChannelMap an
AudioChannelLayout instead of the SInt32 array it takes. macOS 27 rejects
that with -50, mpv treats it as fatal, and the shared coreaudio output never
opens: every track fails with "audio output initialization failed (-14)".
Seen on macOS 27.0 with a Jabra Link 380 (2026-11-04, mpv log: "unable to
set the input channel layout on the audio unit ... /-50"); the exclusive
output (coreaudio_exclusive) doesn't take this path and still played.
Drop this patch once the pinned mpv contains the upstream commit.

